          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Nota del marcador"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Bookmarks" : {
      "comment" : "Heading of the group of bookmark keyboard shortcuts in Settings, and the title of the Bookmarks menu.\nThe name of the bookmarks, wherever it is named: the title of the Bookmarks list over a book's reader (read by VoiceOver as its heading, and the name of its rotor), the reader's Bookmarks toolbar button, and the Bookmarks menu in the menu bar.\nTitle of the Bookmarks menu in the menu bar, which holds the commands that add and move between a book's bookmarks. Only a reader window shows it.\nTitle of the reader toolbar's button that opens the bookmarks sheet.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Marcadores"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Books" : {
      "comment" : "Name of the VoiceOver rotor in the Search Library window that moves between the books that hold matches.\nText of the Folder Settings sheet, which shows one library folder's facts and its listening options. The label of the books in the folder and every folder below it.\nText of the Library view editor sheet, which makes and changes a view of the Library window, and of the descriptions of a view's filter. A kind of row as its checkbox names it: \"Books\", \"Episodes\", \"Articles\", or \"Feeds\". This is the case .books."
    },
    "Books (%lld)" : {
      "comment" : "The header of a list's books, with their count: \"Books (743)\". %lld is the number of books.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "variations" : {
            "plural" : {
              "one" : {
                "stringUnit" : {
                  "state" : "translated",
                  "value" : "Books (%lld)"
                }
              },
              "other" : {
                "stringUnit" : {
                  "state" : "translated",
                  "value" : "Books (%lld)"
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Books with the same title, regardless of author" : {
      "comment" : "Hint of the Same Title criterion of Find Duplicate Books."
    },
    "Braille Code" : {
      "comment" : "Text of Speak Info, Book Information's braille code and text encoding rows, and the re-read alerts. The label of Book Information's row that names a braille book's code, and of its pop-up, which reads the book again with another."
    },
    "Braille File Characters" : {
      "comment" : "Text of Speak Info, Book Information's braille code and text encoding rows, and the re-read alerts. The label of Book Information's pop-up that names the braille file characters a BRF or BRL book's file is read with, in title case, as the sheet's \"Braille Code\" and \"Text Encoding\" are; the Settings and Export pop-ups say \"Braille file characters\", in their own sentence case."
    },
    "Braille characters: %@" : {
      "comment" : "Text of Speak Info, Book Information's braille code and text encoding rows, and the re-read alerts. Speak Info's sentence for braille file characters described as description (Book.brailleFileCodeDescription), said right after the braille code's: \"Braille characters: North American Braille ASCII\". Placeholders in order: description."
    },
    "Braille code: %@" : {
      "comment" : "Speak Info: the part of a braille book's full summary that names its braille code. %@ is the code's description, such as \"Unified English Braille, contracted (Grade 2)\"."
    },
    "Break" : {
      "comment" : "Name of a key of the keyboard, spoken by VoiceOver and shown in braille in a keyboard shortcut such as \"Command + Break\"."
    },
    "But %@ also holds %lld books a newer TextMouth added: they are kept where they are, and so is every folder that holds one." : {
      "comment" : "Last sentence of the second confirmation that deletes a folder, when the folder holds books that a newer TextMouth added. %1$@ is the folder's name in quotation marks and %2$lld is how many books, a count.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "variations" : {
            "plural" : {
              "one" : {
                "stringUnit" : {
                  "state" : "translated",
                  "value" : "But %@ also holds %lld book a newer TextMouth added: it is kept where it is, and so is every folder that holds it."
                }
              },
              "other" : {
                "stringUnit" : {
                  "state" : "translated",
                  "value" : "But %@ also holds %lld books a newer TextMouth added: they are kept where they are, and so is every folder that holds one."
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "By %@" : {
      "comment" : "Speak Info: the part of a book's summary that names its author. %@ is the author's name."
    },
    "Cancel" : {
      "comment" : "Button of a jump panel (Go to Percent, Time or Page) that closes it without jumping.\nButton of the Edit Text explanation alert that stops without opening the editor. Escape presses it.\nButton of the book information sheet that closes it without saving.\nButton that closes a sheet or answers a question without doing or changing anything.\nButton that closes an alert or stops waiting, in the reader.\nButton that leaves a sheet, panel, or question without making its change, such as the panel for adding a bookmark or editing its note.\nText of the Library tab of Settings, a list of the views the Library window offers (built-in views and the listener's own). The button of either question that changes nothing.\nText of the Library view editor sheet, which makes and changes a view of the Library window, and of the descriptions of a view's filter. The button that closes the sheet, changing nothing.\nTitle of a button that cancels, in the Substitutions settings' question and rule editor.\nTitle of the button that cancels the removal of the duplicate books selected, in its confirmation.\nTitle of the question's button that keeps the Record window open; it answers the Escape key.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Cancelar"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Cancel Timer" : {
      "comment" : "Button of the sleep timer sheet that stops the running timer.",
      "localizations" : {
