            "value" : "Todos los libros de arriba en la lista de lectura están terminados"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Every book after it in the folder is finished" : {
      "comment" : "A sentence of the announcement as a book ends, after \"Finished: <title>.\": every book after it in its library folder is finished, so none plays. Written without its full stop.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Todos los libros siguientes de la carpeta están terminados"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Every book before it in the folder is finished" : {
      "comment" : "A sentence of the announcement as a book ends, in a folder or feed that plays the book above: every book before it is finished, so none plays. Written without its full stop.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Todos los libros anteriores de la carpeta están terminados"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Every book below it in the reading list is finished" : {
      "comment" : "A sentence of the announcement as a book read from the reading list ends, after \"Finished: <title>.\": the books below it are all finished, and the list passes over finished books. Written without its full stop.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Todos los libros de abajo en la lista de lectura están terminados"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Every shortcut and where it works go back to the defaults. Your own keys are lost." : {
      "comment" : "Message of the alert that asks the listener to confirm resetting every keyboard shortcut to its default: the shortcuts they changed are lost."
    },
    "Every window" : {
      "comment" : "Choice of the Works in pop-up of a keyboard shortcut: the shortcut works in every window."
    },
    "Everything" : {
      "comment" : "The object of the button that deletes a folder with its contents, in title case, as in \"Move Everything to Trash\"."
    },
    "Everything in %@" : {
      "comment" : "The object of the title of the second confirmation that deletes a folder with its contents, in title case, as in \"Move Everything in “Fiction” to Trash?\". %@ is the folder's name in quotation marks."
    },
    "Exact file content match — the strongest indicator" : {
      "comment" : "Hint of the Identical File criterion of Find Duplicate Books."
    },
    "Exclamation Mark" : {
      "comment" : "Name of the punctuation key \"!\", spoken by VoiceOver and shown in braille in a keyboard shortcut such as \"Command + Exclamation Mark\"."
    },
    "Execute" : {
      "comment" : "Name of a key of the keyboard, spoken by VoiceOver and shown in braille in a keyboard shortcut such as \"Command + Execute\"."
    },
    "Experimental. A sequence of media keys or AirPods controls within a short time window re-arms the last sleep timer, handy after one expires." : {
      "comment" : "Explanation under the Enable restart-timer gesture switch in the Miscellaneous settings. AirPods is a product name and stays as written."
    },
    "Export…" : {
      "comment" : "Name of a keyboard shortcut action, listed in Settings in the audio editor group and read by VoiceOver. Exports the audio to a file."
    },
    "Fade out duration" : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver label of the sleep timer's fade out stepper in the Playback settings."
    },
    "Fade out: %@" : {
      "comment" : "The sleep timer's fade out shown above its stepper in the Playback settings. %@ is the fade as a length of time, such as 3 seconds, or Off."
    },
    "Fading out" : {
      "comment" : "The sleep timer's state while it fades the sound out before pausing, shown in the sleep timer sheet and the reader.",
