    "Greater Than" : {
      "comment" : "Name of the punctuation key \">\", spoken by VoiceOver and shown in braille in a keyboard shortcut such as \"Command + Greater Than\"."
    },
    "Guessed from the book's braille. If it reads wrongly, choose Unified English Braille in Braille Code." : {
      "comment" : "Text of Speak Info, Book Information's braille code and text encoding rows, and the re-read alerts. What Book Information says under the pop-up of a book whose code the import guessed: where the code came from, how to correct it, and how to keep it. Plain and short, so VoiceOver and a braille display read it as it is."
    },
    "Has New Episodes or Articles" : {
      "comment" : "Text of the Library view editor sheet, which makes and changes a view of the Library window, and of the descriptions of a view's filter. A condition's relation as its relation pop-up names it, by its test and whether it is negated. This is the form for the other case of the condition."
    },
    "Has None New" : {
      "comment" : "Text of the Library view editor sheet, which makes and changes a view of the Library window, and of the descriptions of a view's filter. A condition's relation as its relation pop-up names it, by its test and whether it is negated. This is the form for the first case of the condition."
    },
    "Heading" : {
      "comment" : "A unit of text a picker moves or rewinds by: one heading. Used by the rewind, skip, and navigation unit pickers."
    },
    "Heading Levels" : {
      "comment" : "Name of the VoiceOver rotor that moves among the headings of the headings list."
    },
    "Heading info display mode" : {
      "comment" : "What VoiceOver calls the headings sheet's picker that chooses what each heading shows after its name."
