      "comment" : "Name of the application menu's Hide command, in a sentence saying why a keyboard shortcut cannot take its key."
    },
    "Hides jump to page controls" : {
      "comment" : "Hint of the status row's page button while the jump to page panel is open."
    },
    "Hides jump to percent controls" : {
      "comment" : "Hint of the reader's percent button while the jump to percent panel is open."
    },
    "Hides jump to time controls" : {
      "comment" : "Hint of the reader's time button while the jump to time panel is open."
    },
    "Hold Shift while skipping to use a secondary skip amount." : {
      "comment" : "Explanation under the Shift+Skip pop-ups in the Playback settings. Shift is the key's name."
    },
    "Home" : {
      "comment" : "Name of a key of the keyboard, spoken by VoiceOver and shown in braille in a keyboard shortcut such as \"Command + Home\"."
    },
    "How long media commands are blocked after a Bluetooth device disconnects. Raise it if playback resumes after removing headphones." : {
      "comment" : "Explanation under the Bluetooth disconnect delay slider in the Miscellaneous settings."
    },
    "How soon a second press must follow the first. A key with different single and double press actions waits this long before its single press acts." : {
      "comment" : "Hint of the double press time stepper in Settings: what the time is, and that a key that has one action for a single press and another for a double press waits for that time before acting on a single press."
    },
    "ISBN" : {
      "comment" : "Name of the book information sheet's row that shows a book's ISBN, its international book number."
    },
    "ISBN: %@" : {
      "comment" : "The shared value of a group of duplicate books that match by ISBN, in the group's heading. %@ is the ISBN. ISBN stays as written.\nWhat VoiceOver says for the book information sheet's ISBN row. %@ is the book's ISBN."
    },
    "Identical File (MD5)" : {
      "comment" : "A match criterion of Find Duplicate Books: the files' contents are exactly the same. MD5 is the name of the checksum used to compare them."
    },
    "Identifier" : {
      "comment" : "Name of the book information sheet's row that shows a book's identifier, a code that names it."
    },
    "Identifier: %@" : {
      "comment" : "What VoiceOver says for the book information sheet's identifier row. %@ is the book's identifier code."
    },
    "If the file is not written in %@, TextMouth refuses it, and nothing changes." : {
      "comment" : "Text of Speak Info, Book Information's braille code and text encoding rows, and the re-read alerts. What the alert says first of a choice to or from Unicode braille patterns, which the re-read checks byte by byte before it changes anything (BrailleBookReader.requireReadable(_:as:)), so a wrong one is refused at its first line (review of October 30, finding 5): a file not written in the code named codeName, the one chosen, is refused, and nothing changes. \"If the file is not written in Unicode braille patterns, TextMouth refuses it, and nothing changes.\". Placeholders in order: codeName."
    },
    "Ignored When Typing" : {
      "comment" : "A choice of the Leading Articles pop-up: a title's leading article does not count when typing a title's first letters, but the list keeps its order."
    },
    "Ignored When Typing and Sorting" : {
      "comment" : "A choice of the Leading Articles pop-up: a title's leading article does not count when typing or when sorting."
    },
    "Import Folder…" : {
      "comment" : "Name of a keyboard shortcut action, listed in Settings in the Library group and read by VoiceOver. Imports a DAISY book, or a folder of audio tracks, as a book. Also the title of the menu command of the same name."
    },
    "In %@" : {
      "comment" : "Speak Info: the part of a summary that says where a book or a feed's folder is. %@ is the folder's path, such as Fiction/Mystery."
    },
    "In %@, a feed" : {
      "comment" : "Text of Speak Info, Book Information's braille code and text encoding rows, and the re-read alerts. Where an episode or an article is, in the feed titled feedTitle: \"In The Digital Antiquarian, a feed\". Placeholders in order: feedTitle."
    },
    "In Library windows, a letter alone moves to the first book or folder starting with it, so a shortcut that is a letter alone, such as W, works only in other windows." : {
      "comment" : "Note in the Shortcuts tab of Settings. In a Library window, a letter key pressed with no other key jumps to the first book or folder starting with that letter, so a shortcut made of a letter alone, such as W, cannot work in a Library window."
    },
    "In Progress" : {
      "comment" : "Text of the Library view editor sheet, which makes and changes a view of the Library window, and of the descriptions of a view's filter. A reading state as the pop-up names it. This is the case .inProgress."
    },
    "In a regular expression, a dollar sign and a group's number, as in $1 or $2, put back what that group matched." : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver hint of the replacement field in the substitution rule editor. $1 and $2 are written as in regular expressions and stay as written."
    },
    "In reading list" : {
      "comment" : "Part of a library row's VoiceOver label, after the book's title and author: the book is on the reading list.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "En la lista de lectura"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "In reading list, %lld of %lld" : {
      "comment" : "Text of Speak Info, Book Information's braille code and text encoding rows, and the re-read alerts. Where a book in the reading list stands in it, as its brief summary says it, counted as the Reading List shows the list (FR09): \"In reading list, 3 of 12\". Said in every view, the Reading List's own included, where its rows say no more than the list's order does. Placeholders in order: place.position, place.count.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "In reading list, %1$lld of %2$lld"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "In the Reading List" : {
      "comment" : "Text of the Library view editor sheet, which makes and changes a view of the Library window, and of the descriptions of a view's filter. A condition's relation as its relation pop-up names it, by its test and whether it is negated. This is the form for the other case of the condition."
    },
    "In this Mac's Logs folder" : {
      "comment" : "A choice of the Log location pop-up in the Storage settings, and its name inside the pop-up's hint: the diagnostic logs are written in a folder on this Mac that never syncs. The folder's path follows in parentheses where the choice is listed."
    },
    "Include Section" : {
      "comment" : "Name of a heading row's command that stops skipping the section, as a VoiceOver action and a context menu item."
    },
    "Include the speed with time left and total time" : {
      "comment" : "Label of the Playback setting's checkbox that names the speed beside the time left and the total time."
    },
    "Including Subfolders" : {
      "comment" : "Text of the Library view editor sheet, which makes and changes a view of the Library window, and of the descriptions of a view's filter. The subfolders checkbox's visible title."
    },
    "Increase Speed" : {
      "comment" : "Name of a keyboard shortcut action, listed in Settings in the Playback group and read by VoiceOver. Makes the reading speed faster. Also the title of the menu command of the same name."
    },
    "Info: %@" : {
      "comment" : "Navigation title of the book information sheet. %@ is the book's title."
    },
    "Information" : {
      "comment" : "Heading of the group of keyboard shortcuts that speak information, such as Where Am I, in Settings."
    },
    "Insert" : {
      "comment" : "Name of a key of the keyboard, spoken by VoiceOver and shown in braille in a keyboard shortcut such as \"Command + Insert\"."
    },
    "Insert Chapter Marker…" : {
      "comment" : "Name of a keyboard shortcut action, listed in Settings in the audio editor group and read by VoiceOver. Opens a field to name and insert a chapter marker."
    },
    "Insert Character" : {
      "comment" : "Name of a key of the keyboard, spoken by VoiceOver and shown in braille in a keyboard shortcut such as \"Command + Insert Character\"."
    },
    "Insert Line" : {
      "comment" : "Name of a key of the keyboard, spoken by VoiceOver and shown in braille in a keyboard shortcut such as \"Command + Insert Line\"."
    },
    "Insert Silence…" : {
      "comment" : "Name of a keyboard shortcut action, listed in Settings in the audio editor group and read by VoiceOver. Opens a field to type a length of silence to insert."
    },
    "Inside the data directory" : {
      "comment" : "A choice of the Log location pop-up in the Storage settings: the diagnostic logs are written in the Logs folder of the data directory, the folder that holds the library."
    },
    "Invalid regex: %@" : {
      "comment" : "Shown in the substitution rule editor when the pattern is not a valid regular expression. %@ is the reason the system gives, which may be in English. Regex is short for regular expression."
    },
    "Invalid regular expression: %@" : {
      "comment" : "Status line when the search text is not a valid regular expression. %@ is the reason the system gives, which may be in English."
    },
    "Is" : {
      "comment" : "Text of the Library view editor sheet, which makes and changes a view of the Library window, and of the descriptions of a view's filter. A condition's relation as its relation pop-up names it, by its test and whether it is negated. This is the form for the other case of the condition."
    },
    "Is Not" : {
      "comment" : "Text of the Library view editor sheet, which makes and changes a view of the Library window, and of the descriptions of a view's filter. A condition's relation as its relation pop-up names it, by its test and whether it is negated. This is the form for the first case of the condition."
    },
    "It has the same books, places, bookmarks, reading list, and folders." : {
      "comment" : "Sentence of Use This Library's account: the other copy matches the library in use exactly."
    },
    "It holds the folder of the feed %@." : {
      "comment" : "Sentence of the dialog that asks how to delete a folder that holds one feed's folder. %@ is the feed's title in quotation marks."
    },
    "It holds the folders of the feeds %@." : {
      "comment" : "Sentence of the dialog that asks how to delete a folder that holds several feeds' folders. %@ is a list of the feeds' titles in quotation marks."
    },
    "It is the folder of the feed %@: whichever you choose, the feed stays, with its downloads, but no folder lists them until Feed Info gives the feed another folder; Delete Feed… on the feed's row deletes a feed." : {
      "comment" : "Sentence of the dialog that asks how to delete a folder, when it is the folder of one feed. %@ is the feed's title in quotation marks. \"Feed Info\" and \"Delete Feed…\" name a sheet and a command."
    },
    "It is the folder of the feeds %@: whichever you choose, each feed stays, with its downloads, but no folder lists them until Feed Info gives the feed another folder; Delete Feed… on a feed's row deletes a feed." : {
      "comment" : "Sentence of the dialog that asks how to delete a folder, when it is the folder of several feeds. %@ is a list of the feeds' titles in quotation marks. \"Feed Info\" and \"Delete Feed…\" name a sheet and a command."
    },
    "It lists the book's tracks in play order, each with its heading's title. You can reorder, retitle, and group them under headings of your own, and set the pauses between them." : {
      "comment" : "Second sentence of the Edit Manifest explanation: what the manifest lists and what the user can change in it."
    },
    "Its conditions and sort are deleted. The books, episodes, articles, and feeds it lists stay in the library, and a Library window showing it shows another view." : {
      "comment" : "Text of the Library tab of Settings, a list of the views the Library window offers (built-in views and the listener's own). What the question says Delete does, and what it keeps."
    },
    "Its earlier text was kept as %@, in the book's package." : {
      "comment" : "Sentence saying where a backup of a book's earlier text was kept. %@ is a file name such as content.md.edited-20261024T123012Z, which stays as written."
    },
    "Its name, conditions, sort, and limit go back to TextMouth's own. Its place in the list and when it is offered stay as they are." : {
      "comment" : "Text of the Library tab of Settings, a list of the views the Library window offers (built-in views and the listener's own). What the question says Restore Default does, and what it keeps."
    },
    "Its only page is %@." : {
      "comment" : "Second sentence of that message for a book of one page. %@ is that page's label, an identifier written without digit grouping."
    },
    "Its pages run from %@ to %@." : {
      "comment" : "Second sentence of that message. %1$@ is the first page's label and %2$@ the last page's label, identifiers such as i or 300 written without digit grouping.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "Its pages run from %1$@ to %2$@."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Its place, bookmarks, and transcript, if it has any, are kept, and it can be downloaded again." : {
      "comment" : "Sentence about one deleted download: what the listener left in it is kept, and it can be downloaded again."
    },
    "Its text is replaced by the new reading." : {
      "comment" : "Text of Speak Info, Book Information's braille code and text encoding rows, and the re-read alerts. What any re-read does to the book's text."
    },
    "Jump" : {
      "comment" : "Button of a jump panel (Go to Percent, Time or Page) that jumps to what was typed."
    },
    "Jumped to %@ in the recording." : {
      "comment" : "Announcement after Go to Time jumped in an audiobook. %@ is the time spoken in words, such as \"2 hours, 13 minutes, 5 seconds\"."
    },
    "Jumped to %@ percent." : {
      "comment" : "Announcement after Go to Percent jumped. %@ is the percent reached with one decimal place, such as 47.5."
    },
    "Jumped to %@." : {
      "comment" : "Announcement after Go to Time jumped in a text book. %@ is the time spoken in words, such as \"2 hours, 13 minutes, 5 seconds\"."
    },
    "Jumped to page %@, the %@ page labelled %@." : {
      "comment" : "Announcement after Go to Page jumped to one of several pages that carry the same label. %1$@ is the page's label, an identifier; %2$@ is which of them it is, as an ordinal word such as \"second\" or \"11th\".",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "Jumped to page %1$@, the %2$@ page labelled %3$@."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Jumped to page %@." : {
      "comment" : "Announcement after Go to Page jumped. %@ is the page's label, an identifier written without digit grouping."
    },
    "Keep Original" : {
      "comment" : "A choice of the After Importing a Book pop-up in the Storage settings: the original file stays where it was."
    },
    "Keep This Code" : {
      "comment" : "Text of Speak Info, Book Information's braille code and text encoding rows, and the re-read alerts. The label of the button under that note that keeps the guessed code (a pop-up cannot be asked for the choice already selected), and what it does."
    },
    "Keep these books on this Mac" : {
      "comment" : "Checkbox of the Reading List's options bar, shown while the library is in iCloud: keep the list's books downloaded on this Mac.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Conservar estos libros en esta Mac"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Keeps the list's books downloaded on this Mac; each Mac chooses for itself. Clearing it removes no download." : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver hint of the Reading List's Keep these books on this Mac checkbox: a choice of this Mac's alone.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Mantiene descargados en esta Mac los libros de la lista; cada Mac elige por su cuenta. Desmarcarlo no elimina ninguna descarga."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Keeps the order you set with Move Book Up, Move Book Down, or dragging." : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver hint of the Reading List Order item of the Reading List's Sort menu. Move Book Up and Move Book Down are commands of the Library menu.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Mantiene el orden que fijas con Move Book Up, Move Book Down o arrastrando."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Language" : {
      "comment" : "Name of the book information sheet's row that shows the language a book is written in.\nTitle of the pop-up in the Voice settings that narrows the voices to one language, and the label of the selected voice's language beneath it.\nTitle of the voice sheet's menu that limits the voices listed to one language."
    },
    "Language: %@" : {
      "comment" : "What VoiceOver says for the book information sheet's language row. %@ is the language code the book gives, such as en."
    },
    "Last opened %@" : {
      "comment" : "Speak Info: the part of a book's full summary that says when it was last opened. %@ is a date or time, such as \"yesterday\"."
    },
    "Last try: %@" : {
      "comment" : "Text below the Try a Double Press button after a trial ended. %@ is what the trial found, a whole sentence such as \"Double press.\"."
    },
    "Leading articles" : {
      "comment" : "Label of the pop-up in the Library settings that chooses whether a title's leading article (The, A, An) counts when sorting and typing."
    },
    "Left Arrow" : {
      "comment" : "Name of a key of the keyboard, spoken by VoiceOver and shown in braille in a keyboard shortcut such as \"Command + Left Arrow\"."
    },
    "Left Brace" : {
      "comment" : "Name of the punctuation key \"{\", spoken by VoiceOver and shown in braille in a keyboard shortcut such as \"Command + Left Brace\"."
    },
    "Left Bracket" : {
      "comment" : "Name of the punctuation key \"[\", spoken by VoiceOver and shown in braille in a keyboard shortcut such as \"Command + Left Bracket\"."
    },
    "Left Parenthesis" : {
      "comment" : "Name of the punctuation key \"(\", spoken by VoiceOver and shown in braille in a keyboard shortcut such as \"Command + Left Parenthesis\"."
    },
    "Less Than" : {
      "comment" : "Name of the punctuation key \"<\", spoken by VoiceOver and shown in braille in a keyboard shortcut such as \"Command + Less Than\"."
    },
    "Level" : {
      "comment" : "Label of the microphone's loudness while recording, in the Record window."
    },
    "Level 1" : {
      "comment" : "Choice of the headings sheet's level filter that shows only the biggest headings, level 1."
    },
    "Levels 1 to %lld" : {
      "comment" : "Choice of the headings sheet's level filter that shows levels from 1 to a deeper one. %lld is the deepest level shown."
    },
    "Library" : {
      "comment" : "Heading of the group of Library window keyboard shortcuts in Settings, and the title of the Library menu.\nText of the Library tab of Settings, a list of the views the Library window offers (built-in views and the listener's own). The tab's name in the Settings window's toolbar.\nThe top of the library, as the Save in pop-up of the Record window names it.\nTitle of the Library menu in the menu bar, which holds the commands for the library's books and folders. Only a Library window shows it.\nTitle of the first screen, the list of the user's books and folders."
    },
    "Library / %@" : {
      "comment" : "A library folder in the Save in pop-up of the Record window: the library, then the folder's path, its folders separated by slashes. %@ is the path, such as \"Fiction / Sci-Fi\"."
    },
    "Library Root" : {
      "comment" : "The folder name Find Duplicate Books gives a book at the top level of the library, in a duplicate's spoken label."
    },
    "Library windows" : {
      "comment" : "Choice of the Works in pop-up of a keyboard shortcut: the shortcut works in the Library windows, where the library's books are listed.\nNames where a keyboard shortcut works, inside a sentence such as \"Works in Library windows.\": the Library windows, where the library's books are listed."
    },
    "Listening" : {
      "comment" : "Text of the Folder Settings sheet, which shows one library folder's facts and its listening options. The heading over the listening options."
    },
    "Listing %lld matches in %@" : {
      "comment" : "Announcement once Show All has listed every match of a book. %1$lld is the number of matches and %2$@ is the book's title.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "variations" : {
            "plural" : {
              "one" : {
                "stringUnit" : {
                  "state" : "translated",
                  "value" : "Listing %lld match in %@"
                }
              },
              "other" : {
                "stringUnit" : {
                  "state" : "translated",
                  "value" : "Listing %lld matches in %@"
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Listing %lld of %@ matches: refine the search to see the rest" : {
      "comment" : "Row under a book whose matches are more than the list shows even after Show All. %1$lld is the number listed, and %2$@ is the book's total, such as \"700\" or \"more than 1,000\".",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "variations" : {
