                  "value" : "Listing %lld of %@ matches: refine the search to see the rest"
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Listing the first %lld of %@ matches in %@" : {
      "comment" : "Announcement once Show All has listed the first matches of a book that holds more. %1$lld is the number listed, %2$@ is the book's total, such as \"700\" or \"more than 1,000\", and %3$@ is the book's title.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "variations" : {
            "plural" : {
              "one" : {
                "stringUnit" : {
                  "state" : "translated",
                  "value" : "Listing the first %lld of %@ matches in %@"
                }
              },
              "other" : {
                "stringUnit" : {
                  "state" : "translated",
                  "value" : "Listing the first %lld of %@ matches in %@"
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Lists" : {
      "comment" : "Text of the Library view editor sheet, which makes and changes a view of the Library window, and of the descriptions of a view's filter. The label of the checkboxes saying what the view lists."
    },
    "Lists %@" : {
      "comment" : "Library view editor: the start of a filter's description, which says what a view lists. %@ is a list of the kinds it lists in lower case, such as \"books and feeds\". A description ends with a full stop added later."
    },
    "Lists %@." : {
      "comment" : "Library view editor: what the sheet says of a draft view's contents. %@ is a list of counts, such as \"23 books and 2 feeds\"."
    },
    "Lists %@: %@" : {
      "comment" : "Library view editor: the start of a filter's description, which says what a view lists and its conditions. %1$@ is a list of the kinds it lists in lower case, such as \"books and feeds\"; %2$@ is its conditions joined by \"and\" or \"or\". A description ends with a full stop added later.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "Lists %1$@: %2$@"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Lists nothing now." : {
      "comment" : "Library view editor: what the sheet says of a draft view that lists nothing at the moment."
    },
    "Lists up to 500 of this book's matches here" : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver hint of the row that lists a book's matches in the Search Library results. 500 is the most it lists."
    },
    "Loading" : {
      "comment" : "Value of the Play button while the book is loading, spoken by VoiceOver."
    },
    "Loading %@" : {
      "comment" : "What VoiceOver says for the spinner in the reader while a book loads. %@ is the book's title."
    },
    "Loading ISBNs..." : {
      "comment" : "Title of the scan button in Find Duplicate Books while the books' ISBNs are being read first. ISBN stays as written."
    },
    "Loading book..." : {
      "comment" : "Words beside the spinner in the reader while a book loads."
    },
    "Location" : {
      "comment" : "Text of the Folder Settings sheet, which shows one library folder's facts and its listening options. The label of the folder's place: the folder that holds it."
    },
    "Log location" : {
      "comment" : "Label of the pop-up in the Storage settings that chooses where TextMouth writes its diagnostic logs."
    },
    "Logs" : {
      "comment" : "Heading of the Logs group in the Storage settings, which holds the choice of where TextMouth writes its diagnostic logs."
    },
    "Logs are written to %@." : {
      "comment" : "The line under the Log location pop-up in the Storage settings. %@ is the folder's full path, which stays as written."
    },
    "Looks for the book again" : {
      "comment" : "Hint of the Try Again button of the reader's view for a book that the cloud has not yet synced."
    },
    "Loop to Start" : {
      "comment" : "A choice of the When a Book Ends picker: the book plays again from its beginning and is never finished."
    },
    "Made %@, %lld of %lld." : {
      "comment" : "Text of the Library tab of Settings, a list of the views the Library window offers (built-in views and the listener's own). What VoiceOver says after Duplicate: the copy and its place. Placeholders in order: name, number, count.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "Made %1$@, %2$lld of %3$lld."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Make Double Press" : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver action and context menu item of a keyboard shortcut's key button: changes a single press of the key into the key pressed twice quickly."
    },
    "Make Single Press" : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver action and context menu item of a keyboard shortcut's key button: changes a key pressed twice quickly into a single press of the key."
    },
    "Makes a view of your own from the conditions you choose." : {
      "comment" : "Text of the Library view editor sheet, which makes and changes a view of the Library window, and of the descriptions of a view's filter. Its hint."
    },
    "Makes a view of your own with this view's conditions and sort." : {
      "comment" : "Text of the Library tab of Settings, a list of the views the Library window offers (built-in views and the listener's own). Duplicate's hint."
    },
    "Manifest not updated: %@ Fix it in your editor and save again; until then, %@ keeps its headings." : {
      "comment" : "Announcement after an edited manifest.json was refused. %1$@ is the reason, a whole sentence in English that names what is wrong inside the file and may stay in English; %2$@ is the book's title.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "Manifest not updated: %1$@ Fix it in your editor and save again; until then, %2$@ keeps its headings."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Manifest updated" : {
      "comment" : "Announcement after the user saved an edited manifest.json and TextMouth took it as the book's arrangement of tracks."
    },
    "Mark In" : {
      "comment" : "Name of a keyboard shortcut action, listed in Settings in the audio editor group and read by VoiceOver. Starts a selection at the current position."
    },
    "Mark Out" : {
      "comment" : "Name of a keyboard shortcut action, listed in Settings in the audio editor group and read by VoiceOver. Ends the selection at the current position."
    },
    "Markers and Pauses…" : {
      "comment" : "Name of a keyboard shortcut action, listed in Settings in the audio editor group and read by VoiceOver. Opens the list of markers and silent pauses."
    },
    "Match" : {
      "comment" : "Text of the Library view editor sheet, which makes and changes a view of the Library window, and of the descriptions of a view's filter. The match pop-up's label."
    },
    "Match Case" : {
      "comment" : "Title and VoiceOver label of the checkbox in Search in Book and Search Library that makes a match need the search text's capital and small letters."
    },
    "Match criteria (checked filters are combined):" : {
      "comment" : "The line over the checkboxes of Find Duplicate Books that choose how books are matched. Checked criteria must all match together."
    },
    "Match whole word only" : {
      "comment" : "Title and VoiceOver label of the switch in the substitution rule editor that makes the pattern match whole words only."
    },
    "Matches" : {
      "comment" : "Name of the VoiceOver rotor in the Search Library window that moves between the matches listed."
    },
    "Maximum is %@." : {
      "comment" : "Second sentence of that refusal. %@ is the longest time allowed, spoken in words, such as \"1 hour\"."
    },
    "Media-control events that trigger the restart. The last one is consumed, not passed to playback, so it can't start audio." : {
      "comment" : "Explanation under the restart gesture's pattern heading in the Miscellaneous settings."
    },
    "Menu" : {
