    "Quitting TextMouth" : {
      "comment" : "Title of the panel TextMouth shows, and the start of what it says aloud, while it finishes work before quitting."
    },
    "Quitting now leaves these changes unsaved:" : {
      "comment" : "First line of the alert's message when quitting would leave changes unsaved; a list of what is unsaved follows it."
    },
    "Quotation Mark" : {
      "comment" : "Name of the punctuation key \"\"\", spoken by VoiceOver and shown in braille in a keyboard shortcut such as \"Command + Quotation Mark\"."
    },
    "Re-import the book to replace it." : {
      "comment" : "Second sentence of the message when a chapter's audio file is unreadable: what to do."
    },
    "Re-import the book to restore it." : {
      "comment" : "Second sentence of the message when a chapter's audio file is missing: what to do."
    },
    "Read Again" : {
      "comment" : "Text of Speak Info, Book Information's braille code and text encoding rows, and the re-read alerts. The alert's button that reads the book again; Cancel leaves it."
    },
    "Read Only" : {
      "comment" : "Heading of the group of fields of the book information sheet that the user cannot change."
    },
    "Read “%@” again as %@?" : {
      "comment" : "Text of Speak Info, Book Information's braille code and text encoding rows, and the re-read alerts. The title of the alert that asks before the book titled bookTitle is read again as the reading named readingName: \"Read “Ledger” again as Shift JIS (Japanese)?\". Braille file characters are asked about in the same sentence (BrailleFileCodeWording.confirmTitle(bookTitle:code:)). Placeholders in order: bookTitle, readingName.",
      "localizations" : {
