        }
      }
    },
    "Read “%@” again automatically?" : {
      "comment" : "Text of Speak Info, Book Information's braille code and text encoding rows, and the re-read alerts. The title of the alert that asks before a book is read again as option says: \"Read “Ledger” again as Shift JIS (Japanese)?\", or \"Read “Ledger” again automatically?\". Placeholders in order: bookTitle."
    },
    "Reader windows" : {
      "comment" : "Choice of the Works in pop-up of a keyboard shortcut: the shortcut works in the reader windows, where a book is read."
    },
    "Reading List" : {
      "comment" : "Text of the Library view editor sheet, which makes and changes a view of the Library window, and of the descriptions of a view's filter. A kind of test as a condition's test pop-up names it. This is the case .inReadingList.\nThe start of the window title of a book read from the reading list, before a colon and the book's title, in place of \"Book\"; also the name of the Library's Reading List.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Lista de lectura"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Reading List Order" : {
      "comment" : "Name of the order the Reading List shows its books in, the one the listener arranges: the only item of its Sort menu.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Orden de la lista de lectura"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Reading State" : {
      "comment" : "Text of the Library view editor sheet, which makes and changes a view of the Library window, and of the descriptions of a view's filter. A kind of test as a condition's test pop-up names it. This is the case .readingState."
    },
    "Reading list, book %lld of %lld" : {
      "comment" : "Where a book read from the reading list stands in it, in the reader's header and in Where Am I?. %1$lld is the book's place in the list; %2$lld how many books the list holds.",
      "localizations" : {
